       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use under supervision. The OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks:** At this dose, the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events goes up sharply. The risk is higher even when kidney and liver function are normal.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours** for pain or fever.\n- **1600 mg per day in total**, for example 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm the indication and that you've considered the risks. Even then, I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
